method.description:
Returns the paths of the cached resources inside [param directory], in no particular order. A missing trailing slash is added, so [code]"res://levels"[/code] matches [code]res://levels/a.tres[/code] but not [code]res://levels2/a.tres[/code]. The comparison is a case-sensitive string prefix and works with any path prefix, such as [code]res://[/code] or [code]user://[/code].
If [param recursive] is [code]false[/code], only resources directly in [param directory] are returned, not those in its subdirectories. Built-in sub-resources (such as [code]res://levels/a.tscn::Gradient_x1y2z[/code]) belong to the directory of their file.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var level = ResourceLoader.get_cached_paths_in_directory("res://levels/")
var top_level_only = ResourceLoader.get_cached_paths_in_directory("res://levels/", false)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
string[] level = ResourceLoader.GetCachedPathsInDirectory("res://levels/");
string[] topLevelOnly = ResourceLoader.GetCachedPathsInDirectory("res://levels/", false);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[param kinds] limits the result to some kinds of resources, for example [code]CACHED_RESOURCE_KIND_FILE | CACHED_RESOURCE_KIND_BUILT_IN[/code] to leave out imported textures and sounds (see [enum CachedResourceKind]).

Returns how many cached resources there are per class: a [Dictionary] with the class name ([StringName]) as key and the count as value. The class name is the most derived named class of the resource: its global script class ([code]class_name[/code]) if it has one, otherwise its native class. Useful to see what fills the memory.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var counts = ResourceLoader.get_cached_type_counts()
for type in counts:
    print(type, ": ", counts[type])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
foreach (var (type, count) in ResourceLoader.GetCachedTypeCounts())
{
    GD.Print(type, ": ", count);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

Returns the dependencies for the resource at the given [param path].
Each dependency is a string that can be divided into sections by [code]::[/code]. There can be either one section or three sections, with the second section always being empty. When there is one section, it contains the file path. When there are three sections, the first section contains the UID and the third section contains the fallback path.
[codeblock]
for dependency in ResourceLoader.get_dependencies(path):
	if dependency.contains("::"):
		print(dependency.get_slice("::", 0)) # Prints the UID.
		print(dependency.get_slice("::", 2)) # Prints the fallback path.
	else:
		print(dependency) # Prints the path.
[/codeblock]

Loads all resources described by [param manifest] (see [method get_manifest_paths]) on the calling thread and returns a [Dictionary] that maps each path to its [Resource]. Paths that fail to load print an error and are left out. If [member FilesManifest.type_hint] is a built-in class, it is passed to the loaders as type hint.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var manifest: FilesManifest = load("res://data/items.tres")
var items := ResourceLoader.load_manifest(manifest)
for path in items:
	print(path, ": ", items[path])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var manifest = GD.Load<FilesManifest>("res://data/items.tres");
Godot.Collections.Dictionary items = ResourceLoader.LoadManifest(manifest);
foreach (var (path, resource) in items)
{
    GD.Print(path, ": ", resource);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

Loads a resource like [method load] and reports why it failed: the returned [ResourceLoadResult] holds the resource, or the [enum Error] code and the message the loader printed. The resource is the same (cached) instance that [method load] returns.
[member ResourceLoadResult.error] is [constant ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND] if there is no file at [param path] (whatever code the loader returned), [constant ERR_INVALID_DATA] if the loaded resource is not a [param type_hint] (a native class or a global script class), otherwise the code of the loader. [member ResourceLoadResult.error_message] holds the errors printed while the resource and its dependencies were loaded, also on worker threads; if nothing was printed, the name of the error code and the path. The errors are still printed as with [method load].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var result := ResourceLoader.load_result("res://data/items.tres")
if not result.ok:
	push_error(result.error_message)
	return
var items: Resource = result.resource
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
ResourceLoadResult result = ResourceLoader.LoadResult("res://data/items.tres");
if (!result.Ok)
{
    GD.PushError(result.ErrorMessage);
    return;
}
Resource items = result.Resource;
// Shorter, with a type check: ResourceLoader.TryLoad<T>().
if (ResourceLoader.TryLoad<Texture2D>("res://icon.svg", out Texture2D icon, out Error error))
{
    GD.Print(icon.GetSize());
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

Returns the progress of loading the files of [param manifest] that [method load_threaded_request_manifest] requested: files loaded, total files and the ratio, which includes the progress of the files that are still loading. It only asks, on every platform: it never requests or loads a file, and after [method load_threaded_get_manifest] took the resources it reports no loaded files (it does not load them again). Call it every frame (for example for a "n / X loaded" label and a progress bar), then use [method load_threaded_get_manifest] when [method LoadProgress.is_finished] is [code]true[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] Without thread support (the default Web export) the files do not load by themselves: call [method load_threaded_step_manifest] every frame instead, it loads one more file per call and returns the same progress.
[b]Note:[/b] Call it from the main thread only. The manifest resolves its paths once per request.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
    ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request_manifest(manifest)

func _process(_delta):
    var progress := ResourceLoader.load_threaded_step_manifest(manifest)
    $Label.text = "%d / %d loaded" % [progress.get_loaded_count(), progress.get_total_count()]
    if progress.is_finished():
        var resources := ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_manifest(manifest)
        set_process(false)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Process(double delta)
{
    LoadProgress progress = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedStepManifest(manifest);
    GetNode<Label>("Label").Text = $"{progress.GetLoadedCount()} / {progress.GetTotalCount()} loaded";
    if (progress.IsFinished())
    {
        Godot.Collections.Dictionary resources = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetManifest(manifest);
        SetProcess(false);
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]

Starts a threaded load (see [method load_threaded_request]) for every path described by [param manifest]. Query the progress of each path with [method load_threaded_get_status] and get the resources with [method load_threaded_get], using the paths returned by [method get_manifest_paths]. [b]Note:[/b] Without thread support (the default Web export) this loads nothing yet: advance the load with [method load_threaded_step_manifest]. Returns [constant OK] if all requests were started, otherwise the first error; the other paths are still requested.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var paths := ResourceLoader.get_manifest_paths(manifest)
ResourceLoader.load_threaded_request_manifest(manifest)
# Later, for example in _process():
for path in paths:
	if ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_status(path) == ResourceLoader.THREAD_LOAD_LOADED:
		var resource := ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get(path)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
string[] paths = ResourceLoader.GetManifestPaths(manifest);
ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequestManifest(manifest);
// Later, for example in _Process():
foreach (string path in paths)
{
    if (ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus(path) == ResourceLoader.ThreadLoadStatus.Loaded)
    {
        Resource resource = ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGet(path);
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In builds without threads (the default Web export), the worker thread pool runs each request on the calling thread, so this method blocks until all resources are loaded, like [method load_manifest].

Registers a simple resource format with one call: files whose name ends with [param extension] are loaded by calling [param loader], without writing a [ResourceFormatLoader]. Use [method ResourceSaver.register_extension_saver] to save files of the same format.
[param extension] is given without the leading dot and is compared case-insensitively; it may contain dots, for example [code]"quiz.json"[/code]. [param loader] receives the path of the file ([code]func(path: String)[/code]) and returns the loaded [Resource], or an [enum Error] code if loading fails. If it returns [constant ERR_FILE_UNRECOGNIZED], the file is handed to the next loader that recognizes it, without an error message.
[param type] is the class of the loaded resources: a [Resource] class or a global script class ([code]class_name[/code]) that extends [Resource]. A load with a type hint only uses this format if [param type] is the hint or inherits it, and [method get_resource_type] reports [param type] (or the native base class of a script class). If [param at_front] is [code]true[/code], the format is asked before all other registered loaders, so it can take over extensions of other formats.
Registering an extension again replaces the previous [Callable]. Returns [constant OK], or [constant ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER] if the extension, the callable or the type is not valid.
The format behaves like any other [ResourceFormatLoader]: loaded resources are cached as with [method load], and [method load_threaded_request] works as well. No [code].uid[/code] files are used for these files.
[b]Note:[/b] [param loader] returns a [Variant] (a [Resource] or an [enum Error] code) for the same reason as [method ResourceFormatLoader._load]: script functions have no out-parameters, and the binding layer cannot return a C++ struct. Callers of [method load] who need the code and the message use [method load_result].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	ResourceLoader.register_extension_loader("quiz", _load_quiz, &"QuizSet")
	var quiz: QuizSet = load("res://questions.quiz")

static func _load_quiz(path: String) -> Variant:
	var file := FileAccess.open(path, FileAccess.READ)
	if file == null:
		return FileAccess.get_open_error()
	var quiz := QuizSet.new()
	quiz.questions = file.get_as_text().split("\n", false)
	return quiz
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
	ResourceLoader.RegisterExtensionLoader("quiz", Callable.From<string, Variant>(LoadQuiz), "QuizSet");
	var quiz = GD.Load<QuizSet>("res://questions.quiz");
}

private static Variant LoadQuiz(string path)
{
	using var file = FileAccess.Open(path, FileAccess.ModeFlags.Read);
	if (file == null)
	{
		return (int)FileAccess.GetOpenError();
	}
	var quiz = new QuizSet();
	quiz.Questions = file.GetAsText().Split('\n', System.StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);
	return quiz;
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] [param loader] is called on the thread that loads the file. With [method load_threaded_request], this is a worker thread, so [param loader] must be safe to call from other threads; a static function that only reads the file is. No engine lock is held while [param loader] runs. In the single-threaded Web export, it always runs on the main thread.
[b]Note:[/b] If the object that [param loader] is bound to is freed, loading fails with an error. Call [method unregister_extension_loader] before freeing it. All registrations are removed when the engine shuts down.
